  "question": {
    "text": "Given that the slope of the tangent to a curve <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> at any point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;If the curve passes through the centre of the circle <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then its equation is",
